    "note": "First course sidecar for the fuehrerschein module (which had no course layer at all before this file) and the first shipped content anywhere in this repo to use section_kind \"media\" - see docs/course-media-sections.md. Six sections are media/image sections pointing at app/assets/diagrams/kurs-vorfahrt-0*.svg, generated by assets/generate_vorfahrt_scenarios.py (a separate script from generate_signs.py and generate_diagrams.py on purpose: AGENTS.md forbids concurrent edits to the former, and the latter owns the per-QUESTION vorfahrt-NN[-answer].svg diagrams referenced from image_ref). Lesson fs-l3 carries lesson_kind \"guidance\" with completion_rule \"read\" and no select block, the same pattern aevo introduced: it is written background on the examination FORMAT (the film-sequence tasks the real theory test has contained since 1 April 2014), which the question bank cannot honestly test with a still image. A video_mp4 media section is the intended slot for real footage once the PO supplies it; nothing here fakes it in the meantime.",
    "legal_review_status": "NOT legally reviewed. Every scenario's stated answer was derived this session from the current text of the StVO on gesetze-im-internet.de - §§ 1, 2, 8, 9, 25, 26, 36 and 37 - and from §§ 16 and Anlage 7 Teil 1 FeV, and the governing sentences are quoted inline in each section so a reviewer can check the derivation rather than the conclusion. Deliberately NOT sourced from any official Fragenkatalog, from any exam-prep or driving-school material, or from general recollection of driving-school teaching. Two points a reviewer should look at specifically. (1) fs-l2-s2 (scenario 5): the claim that a cyclist who RIDES across a Fussgaengerueberweg gains no priority from § 26 Abs. 1 rests on that sentence's closed enumeration - \"zu Fuss Gehenden sowie Fahrenden von Krankenfahrstuehlen oder Rollstuehlen\" - and not on case law, which has not been reviewed here; the section is careful to add that § 1 Abs. 2 StVO still forbids driving at the cyclist. (2) fs-l2-s3 (scenario 6): the ordering C/D before A before B assumes an intersection with no Zeichen 205/206/301/306, no Lichtzeichenanlage, no police officer and no Feld- or Waldweg; that assumption is stated in the section's own text because § 8 Abs. 1 Satz 2 StVO would change the A/B half of the answer if it did not hold. The number of video tasks per examination (two) and the number of replays (five) are examination PRACTICE, not FeV text: § 16 Abs. 2 FeV only authorises \"unterschiedliche Medien\" and refers the detail to Anlage 7 Teil 1 and thence to the Pruefungsrichtlinie published in the Verkehrsblatt (document O 3210), which is a paid publication and was NOT read for this round - the section says so and tells the learner the directive governs, not the summary. All six diagrams are original schematic drawings; none traces or imitates any official Fragenkatalog image, ADAC artwork or third-party driving-school illustration.",
